# UNOPS Opportunity+ System - Angular Component Development Guidelines

Comprehensive development guidelines for Angular components in the UNOPS Opportunity+ Partnership and Opportunity Management System.

This application (`UNOPS.PAO.ClientApp`) is a comprehensive partnership management platform built with Angular 19, featuring:
- **Partnership Management**: Organizations, contacts, interactions, and relationship tracking
- **Opportunity Management**: Business opportunity pipeline and tracking
- **Administration**: Entity management, user management, translation workbench
- **AI Integration**: AI assistant with prompt management and content generation
- **Advanced Search**: Cross-entity search capabilities

The application is built using modern Angular 19 signals architecture with Tailwind-first styling and PrimeNG components.

Based on established patterns and the actual project structure.

## Component Creation & Structure

### **Naming Convention & Folder Structure**

**MANDATORY**: Follow this consistent naming and folder organization pattern for all entity components.

**CRITICAL**: All folder and file names MUST use **kebab-case** (Angular 19 convention).

**Pattern Structure:**
```
entity-name/                                  # Main entity folder (kebab-case)
├── entity-name.component.ts                  # List/overview component
├── entity-name.component.html
├── entity-name.component.scss
├── entity-name-item/                         # Detail component folder
│   ├── entity-name-item.component.ts
│   ├── entity-name-item.component.html
│   └── entity-name-item.component.scss
├── new-entity-name/                          # Create dialog component folder
│   ├── new-entity-name.component.ts
│   ├── new-entity-name.component.html
│   └── new-entity-name.component.scss
├── delete-entity-name/                       # Other dialog components (directly in entity folder)
│   ├── delete-entity-name.component.ts       # Dialog names include entity name
│   ├── delete-entity-name.component.html
│   └── delete-entity-name.component.scss
├── custom-action-entity-name/                # Custom action dialogs with entity name
│   ├── custom-action-entity-name.component.ts
│   ├── custom-action-entity-name.component.html
│   └── custom-action-entity-name.component.scss
└── child-entity/                             # Child entities (recursive pattern, kebab-case)
    ├── child-entity.component.ts             # Child list component
    ├── child-entity.component.html
    ├── child-entity-item/                    # Child detail component
    │   └── child-entity-item.component.ts
    ├── new-child-entity/                     # Child create dialog
    │   └── new-child-entity.component.ts
    └── delete-child-entity/                  # Child entity dialogs (directly in child folder)
        └── delete-child-entity.component.ts
```

**Real-World Example - Partner Entity:**
```
partner/
├── partner.component.ts                      # Partner list component
├── partner.component.html
├── partner.component.scss
├── partner-item/                             # Partner detail component
│   ├── partner-item.component.ts
│   ├── partner-item.component.html
│   └── partner-item.component.scss
├── new-partner/                              # Create partner dialog
│   ├── new-partner.component.ts
│   ├── new-partner.component.html
│   └── new-partner.component.scss
├── delete-partner/
│   ├── delete-partner.component.ts
│   └── delete-partner.component.html
└── contacts/                                 # Child entity (recursive)
    ├── contacts.component.ts                 # Contact list component
    ├── contacts.component.html
    ├── contact-item/                         # Contact detail component
    │   ├── contact-item.component.ts
    │   └── contact-item.component.html
    ├── new-contact/                          # Create contact dialog
    │   └── new-contact.component.ts
    └── delete-contact/                       # Contact dialogs (directly in contact folder)
        └── delete-contact.component.ts
```

**Naming Rules:**

**CRITICAL**: All names use **kebab-case** format (lowercase with hyphens).

1. **List Component**: `entity-name.component.ts`
   - Same name as parent folder (kebab-case)
   - Example: `partner/partner.component.ts`
   - Example: `opportunity/opportunity.component.ts`
   - Selector: `app-entity-name` (e.g., `app-partner`, `app-opportunity`)

2. **Detail Component**: `entity-name-item/entity-name-item.component.ts`
   - Folder name: `entity-name-item` (kebab-case)
   - Component name: `entity-name-item.component.ts`
   - Example: `partner/partner-item/partner-item.component.ts`
   - Example: `opportunity/opportunity-item/opportunity-item.component.ts`
   - Selector: `app-entity-name-item` (e.g., `app-partner-item`)

3. **Create Dialog**: `new-entity-name/new-entity-name.component.ts`
   - Folder name: `new-entity-name` (kebab-case with 'new-' prefix)
   - Component name: `new-entity-name.component.ts`
   - Example: `partner/new-partner/new-partner.component.ts`
   - Selector: `app-new-entity-name` (e.g., `app-new-partner`)

4. **Other Dialogs**: `action-entity-name/action-entity-name.component.ts`
   - **CRITICAL**: Dialog names MUST include the entity name (not generic names)
   - Folder directly in entity folder (not in `dialogs/` subfolder)
   - Pattern: `{action}-{entity-name}` in kebab-case
   - Example: `partner/delete-partner/delete-partner.component.ts` (NOT `delete-confirmation-dialog`)
   - Selector: `app-action-entity-name` (e.g., `app-delete-partner`)
   - **Note**: Edit functionality is handled by `entity-name-item` component, not a separate dialog

5. **Child Entities**: Follow same pattern recursively inside parent folder (kebab-case)
   - Example: `partner/contacts/` follows full pattern
   - Example: `opportunity/opportunity-documents/` follows full pattern

**Component Selector Naming:**
- Always prefix with `app-`
- Use kebab-case matching folder/file name
- Examples:
  - `partner.component.ts` → selector: `app-partner`
  - `partner-item.component.ts` → selector: `app-partner-item`
  - `new-partner.component.ts` → selector: `app-new-partner`
  - `delete-partner.component.ts` → selector: `app-delete-partner`
  - `opportunity.component.ts` → selector: `app-opportunity`

