## 🔐 Permission Handling

### **MANDATORY: Server-Side Permission Checks Only**

**CRITICAL**: NEVER manually handle permissions on the client side. ALL permission checks must be performed server-side via dedicated permission endpoints.

**Why This Matters:**
- ✅ **Security**: Client-side checks can be bypassed - server is the source of truth
- ✅ **Consistency**: Same permission logic across all features
- ✅ **Maintainability**: Permission logic changes in one place (backend)
- ✅ **Authorization**: Permissions respect user roles, entity state, and business rules

### **Correct Pattern - Server-Side Permission Endpoint**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Component TypeScript
export class PartnerItemComponent implements OnInit {
  // Permission state from server
  readonly recordPermissions = signal<any>(null);
  readonly permissionsLoading = signal<boolean>(false);
  
  // Computed permissions for UI
  readonly canEdit = computed(() => this.recordPermissions()?.canEdit === true);
  readonly canDelete = computed(() => this.recordPermissions()?.canDelete === true);
  readonly canChangeStage = computed(() => {
    const permissions = this.recordPermissions();
    return permissions?.canActivate === true || permissions?.canCancel === true;
  });
  
  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.loadRecord();
    this.loadPermissions();  // Load permissions from server
  }
  
  /**
   * @description Load permissions from server endpoint
   */
  private loadPermissions(): void {
    this.permissionsLoading.set(true);
    
    this.partnerService.getRecordDetailPermissionsById(this.recordId).subscribe({
      next: (data: any) => {
        this.recordPermissions.set(data);
        this.permissionsLoading.set(false);
      },
      error: () => {
        this.permissionsLoading.set(false);
      }
    });
  }
}
```

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Service with permission endpoint
export class PartnerService {
  /**
   * @description Get record-level permissions from server
   * @param {string} recordId - Record ID
   * @returns {Observable<any>} Observable of permissions object
   */
  getRecordDetailPermissionsById(recordId: string): Observable<any> {
    this.isLoading.set(true);
    return this.http.get(`/api/partner/${recordId}/permissions`).pipe(
      tap({
        next: () => this.isLoading.set(false),
        error: () => this.isLoading.set(false)
      })
    );
  }
}
```

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Use computed permissions in template -->
<div class="flex gap-2">
  @if (canEdit()) {
    <p-button
      [label]="'button.edit' | translate"
      icon="pi pi-pencil"
      severity="primary"
      (onClick)="onEdit()"
    />
  }
  
  @if (canDelete()) {
    <p-button
      [label]="'button.delete' | translate"
      icon="pi pi-trash"
      severity="danger"
      (onClick)="onDelete()"
    />
  }
</div>
```

### **Incorrect Patterns - DO NOT DO THIS**

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Manual client-side permission logic
export class MyComponent {
  canEdit = computed(() => {
    // ❌ Never manually check roles or status client-side
    const currentUser = this.authService.currentUser();
    const isOwner = this.record()?.createdBy === currentUser.id;
    const isDraft = this.record()?.stage === 'Draft';
    return isOwner && isDraft;  // ❌ This bypasses server authorization
  });
}

// ❌ WRONG - Hardcoded permission flags
export class MyComponent {
  canEdit = signal(true);  // ❌ Never hardcode permissions
  canDelete = signal(false);
}

// ❌ WRONG - Role-based checks in component
export class MyComponent {
  canApprove = computed(() => {
    // ❌ Don't check roles directly in components
    return this.authService.hasRole('Administrator');
  });
}
```

### **Permission Endpoint Pattern**

**Standard Permission Endpoint URL:**
```
GET /api/{entity-name}/{recordId}/permissions
```

**Examples:**
- `/api/partner/{id}/permissions`
- `/api/contact/{id}/permissions`
- `/api/opportunity/{id}/permissions`
- `/api/interaction/{id}/permissions`

**Standard Permission Response:**
```json
{
  "canEdit": true,
  "canDelete": false,
  "canSubmit": true,
  "canApprove": false,
  "canActivate": true,
  "canCancel": false,
  "canReview": true
}
```

**Permission flags vary by entity** - each entity defines its own permission structure based on business rules.

### **Permission Loading Best Practices**

1. **Load on Component Init**: Call `loadPermissions()` in `ngOnInit()`
2. **Reload After Actions**: Reload permissions after state-changing actions (submit, approve, etc.)
3. **Use Computed Signals**: Create computed signals for cleaner template usage
4. **Handle Loading States**: Show loading skeletons while permissions load
5. **Cache on Signal**: Store permissions in a signal for reactive updates

### **Permission Integration Checklist**

When adding permissions to a component:

- [ ] Add `recordPermissions` signal to store server response
- [ ] Add `permissionsLoading` signal for loading state
- [ ] Create computed signals for each permission flag (`canEdit`, `canDelete`, etc.)
- [ ] Add service method `getRecordDetailPermissionsById(recordId: string)`
- [ ] Call `loadPermissions()` in `ngOnInit()`
- [ ] Reload permissions after state-changing actions
- [ ] Use computed permission signals in template with `@if` conditions
- [ ] **NEVER** manually check roles, user ID, or entity state for permissions
- [ ] **NEVER** hardcode permission flags
- [ ] **ALWAYS** get permissions from server endpoint

