## 🔄 Workflow Component Usage

### **MANDATORY: Use Workflow Component for All Workflow-Related UI**

**CRITICAL**: Always use the `app-workflow` component for displaying workflow stages and actions. NEVER create separate buttons or display stage status independently.

**Why This Matters:**
- ✅ **Consistency**: All workflow UI follows the same pattern across the application
- ✅ **Maintainability**: Workflow logic centralized in one component
- ✅ **User Experience**: Users see familiar workflow patterns everywhere
- ✅ **Permission Handling**: Workflow component handles permission checks automatically
- ✅ **Action Integration**: Stage display and available actions are coupled correctly

### **Correct Pattern - Use app-workflow Component**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Component TypeScript
import { WorkflowComponent } from '@/shared/reusables/components/workflow/workflow.component';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-opportunity-item',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [
    // ... other imports
    WorkflowComponent,  // Import workflow component
  ],
  templateUrl: './opportunity-item.component.html',
})
export class OpportunityItemComponent implements OnInit {
  // Entity identifiers
  opportunityId = signal<number>(0);
  
  // Permission flags
  readonly canChangeStage = signal<boolean>(false);
  
  ngOnInit(): void {
    // Load entity data
    this.loadOpportunity();
  }
  
  // Handle successful stage change
  handleStageChangeSuccess(): void {
    // Reload entity data after workflow action
    this.loadOpportunity();
  }
  
  // Optional: Hook before stage change for validation
  beforeStageChange = async (nextStage: string): Promise<boolean> => {
    // Perform validation or checks before allowing stage change
    if (this.hasUnsavedChanges()) {
      const confirmed = await this.feedbackService.confirm({
        title: 'Unsaved Changes',
        message: 'You have unsaved changes. Do you want to continue?'
      });
      return confirmed;
    }
    return true;
  };
}
```

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Component Template -->
@if (!isLoading()) {
  <app-workflow
    [entityName]="'opportunity'"
    [entityId]="opportunityId().toString()"
    [canChangeStage]="canChangeStage()"
    [beforeStageChange]="beforeStageChange"
    (onStageChangeSuccess)="handleStageChangeSuccess()"
  />
}
```

### **Component Inputs and Outputs**

**Required Inputs:**
- `entityName` (string): The entity type identifier (e.g., `'opportunity'`, `'partner'`)
- `entityId` (string): The unique identifier of the entity instance (must be converted to string)

**Optional Inputs:**
- `canChangeStage` (boolean): Whether the user can perform workflow actions (default: `true`)
- `beforeStageChange` (function): Async callback hook executed before stage change for validation
  - Signature: `(nextStage: string) => Promise<boolean>`
  - Return `true` to allow stage change, `false` to prevent it

**Outputs:**
- `onStageChangeSuccess`: Event emitted when a workflow stage change is completed successfully

### **When to Use Workflow Component**

Use `app-workflow` for any entity that has:
- ✅ Multiple workflow stages (Draft, Active, Inactive, etc.)
- ✅ Workflow actions (Activate, Deactivate, Archive, etc.)
- ✅ Permission-based access to workflow actions
- ✅ Status tracking

### **Dialog Components - Separation Pattern**

**MANDATORY**: All dialogs (`p-dialog`) must be extracted into separate dedicated dialog components.

**Why Separate Dialog Components:**
- ✅ **Single Responsibility**: Each component has one clear purpose
- ✅ **Reusability**: Dialog logic can be reused across multiple parent components
- ✅ **Testability**: Dialogs can be tested in isolation
- ✅ **Maintainability**: Easier to locate and modify dialog-specific logic
- ✅ **Code Organization**: Cleaner parent components with less clutter

**Pattern:**

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Dialog embedded in parent component
@Component({
  selector: 'app-partner-list',
  template: `
    <div>
      <!-- List content -->
      <p-button (onClick)="showDialog = true" />
      
      <!-- ❌ Dialog inline in parent component -->
      <p-dialog [(visible)]="showDialog">
        <form>
          <!-- Complex dialog content -->
        </form>
      </p-dialog>
    </div>
  `
})
export class PartnerListComponent {
  showDialog = false;
  formData = {};
  // Dialog-specific logic mixed with list logic
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Dialog in separate component
@Component({
  selector: 'app-new-partner',
  template: `
    <p-dialog 
      [(visible)]="visible" 
      (onHide)="visibleChange.emit(false)">
      <form [formGroup]="form" (ngSubmit)="onSubmit()">
        <!-- Dialog content -->
      </form>
    </p-dialog>
  `
})
export class NewPartnerComponent {
  readonly visible = model<boolean>(false);
  readonly partnerCreated = output<PartnerModel>();
  
  // Dialog-specific logic isolated
}

// Parent component
@Component({
  selector: 'app-partner-list',
  template: `
    <div>
      <!-- List content -->
      <p-button (onClick)="showCreateDialog = true" />
      
      <!-- ✅ Dialog as separate component -->
      <app-new-partner
        [(visible)]="showCreateDialog"
        (partnerCreated)="onPartnerCreated($event)"
      />
    </div>
  `
})
export class PartnerListComponent {
  showCreateDialog = false;
  
  onPartnerCreated(partner: PartnerModel) {
    // Handle successful creation
    this.loadPartners();
    this.navigateTo(partner.id);
  }
}
```

**Dialog Component Structure:**

```
feature-folder/
├── entity-name/
│   ├── entity-name.component.ts
│   ├── entity-name.component.html
│   ├── entity-name.component.scss
│   ├── new-entity-name/                      # Dialog components directly in entity folder
│   │   ├── new-entity-name.component.ts     # Dialog names include entity name
│   │   ├── new-entity-name.component.html
│   │   └── new-entity-name.component.scss
│   └── delete-entity-name/
│       ├── delete-entity-name.component.ts
│       ├── delete-entity-name.component.html
│       └── delete-entity-name.component.scss
```

**When to Create Separate Dialog Components:**
- ✅ Always - every `p-dialog` should be in its own component
- ✅ Create, Edit, Delete confirmation dialogs
- ✅ Complex forms in dialogs
- ✅ Multi-step wizards
- ✅ Any dialog with validation logic
- ✅ Dialogs that may be reused elsewhere

**Exception:**
- ❌ Very simple confirmation dialogs that just call a method (use FeedbackService instead)

