## 📋 User Feedback & Confirmation Patterns

### **Confirmation Dialogs**

**MANDATORY**: Use the feedback service for user confirmations, NOT browser `alert()`, `confirm()`, or `prompt()`.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use feedback service
import { FeedbackDialogService } from '@/shared/services/feedback-dialog.service';

export class MyComponent {
  private readonly feedbackService = inject(FeedbackDialogService);
  
  handleDelete() {
    this.feedbackService.showConfirmDialog(
      {
        summary: 'Delete Item',
        detail: 'Are you sure you want to delete this item? This action cannot be undone.',
      },
      () => {
        // User confirmed - proceed with deletion
        this.deleteItem();
        
        // Show success feedback
        this.feedbackService.showSuccessToast({
          summary: 'Success',
          detail: 'Item deleted successfully'
        });
      }
    );
  }
}

// ❌ WRONG - Don't use browser dialogs
handleDelete() {
  if (confirm('Are you sure you want to delete this item?')) {
    this.deleteItem();
    alert('Item deleted successfully');
  }
}
```

### **❌ DON'T Handle HTTP Errors Locally**

**MANDATORY**: Use the global HTTP error handler instead of local error handling in components.

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Local HTTP error handling
this.partnerService.createPartner(requestJson).subscribe({
  next: (data: any) => {
    this.feedbackService.showSuccessToast({ summary: 'Success', detail: 'Partner created!' });
    this.loadData();
  },
  error: (error: any) => {
    console.error('Error creating partner:', error);
    this.feedbackService.showErrorToast({ summary: 'Error', detail: 'Failed to create partner.' });
  }
});

// ✅ CORRECT - Let global error handler manage HTTP errors
this.partnerService.createPartner(requestJson).subscribe({
  next: (data: any) => {
    this.feedbackService.showSuccessToast({ summary: 'Success', detail: 'Partner created!' });
    this.loadData();
  }
  // No error handler - global HTTP interceptor handles all HTTP errors
});
```

